{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"AutomaticScreenTracking"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"AutomaticScreenTracking"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this module when an app’s screens should track their own views: on iOS, iPadOS, tvOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"visionOS and Mac Catalyst through a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIWindowScene"},{"text":", and on macOS through an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSWindow"},{"text":". On","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"watchOS and Linux it builds empty. To track one screen by hand, or a view a macOS","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStack"},{"text":" pushes, give it ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreen(_:)"},{"text":" from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing is tracked until a window scene or a window turns it on with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreensAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A screen is a view controller on screen none of whose children is: the one a navigation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"controller shows, a tab’s, one presented. It tracks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenViewed"},{"type":"text","text":" once as it appears, and again"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when it reappears after being covered or hidden. The screen is named after its controller’s type,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or for a hosting controller after the type of the SwiftUI view it shows. The closure gets each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiscoveredScreen"},{"type":"text","text":" and returns the event to track, renamed, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" to skip the screen:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ In the scene delegate's scene(_:willConnectTo:options:), beside the scene's tracker:","windowScene.traitOverrides.tracker = tracker","windowScene.trackScreensAutomatically { screen in","    screen.name == \"DebugMenuViewController\" ? nil : ScreenViewed(screen: screen.name)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On macOS, a window turns it on, and each screen view goes through the tracker the screen’s view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"finds up its responder chain (","type":"text"},{"code":"NSView.tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import AppKit","import SwiftUI","","struct PreferencesView: View {","    var body: some View {","        Text(\"Preferences\")","    }","}","","final class PreferencesWindowController: NSWindowController, TrackerProviding {","    let tracker: Tracker","","    init(tracker: Tracker) {","        self.tracker = tracker","        super.init(window: NSWindow(contentViewController: NSHostingController(rootView: PreferencesView())))","    }","","    required init?(coder: NSCoder) { nil }","}","","let controller = PreferencesWindowController(tracker: tracker)","controller.window?.trackScreensAutomatically()  \/\/ tracks ScreenViewed(screen: \"PreferencesView\")","controller.showWindow(nil)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"kinds:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" limits tracking to UIKit’s (or AppKit’s) view controllers or to SwiftUI’s views. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI screen given ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left to that modifier, so it isn’t tracked twice.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Discovery looks after each turn of the main run loop, swizzles nothing, and touches no other scene","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or window. On a UIKit platform, each screen view goes through the tracker the screen’s traits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hold, so each scene keeps its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This documentation is built on macOS, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIWindowScene","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreensAutomatically(kinds:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"stopTrackingScreensAutomatically()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" have no pages here; they take the same parameters as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSWindow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s, with ","type":"text"},{"code":"kinds:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" defaulting to ","type":"text"},{"code":"[.uiKit, .swiftUI]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and their doc comments are in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sources.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"also covers control activations and the app’s lifecycle.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"API","text":"API","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where this module’s API isn’t there, so its symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have no pages of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for an Apple target.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Tracking-a-windows-screens","text":"Tracking a window’s screens","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSWindow.trackScreensAutomatically(kinds:_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSWindow.stopTrackingScreensAutomatically()"}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Naming-screens","text":"Naming screens","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DiscoveredScreen","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DiscoveredScreen.Kind","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Track a screen view each time a screen’s view controller appears, without a modifier or a call on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each screen.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"type":"topic","title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track a screen view each time a screen’s view controller appears, without a modifier or a call on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each screen."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","identifier":